 "postReviewDelta": "Review findings fixed: F1 owned backup directories are ordered by their embedded stamp (backup-lib.zsh owned_backups_chronological; rollback default pick and prune_backups use it); F2 a failed undo swap preserves the other writer's bytes beside the file and reports concurrentEditUndoFailed (PrivateIntegrationFile.replace, json-config.swift commit); F3 install/uninstall undo() runs with errexit off and reports restore-failed with the recovery command, rollback wraps its apply phase in a trap that puts the saved state back. Regression tests: testDefaultRollbackAndPruningFollowTheStampNotTheNamePrefix, testARestoreFailureInsideUndoIsReportedAndKeepsTheBackup, testRollbackApplyFailurePutsThePreviousStateBack, testFailedUndoSwapPreservesTheOtherWritersBytesAndSaysSo."
